{
  "dom_id": "step-q213407",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following integers has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27?$\n\n- $11$\n- $16$\n- $23$",
  "worked_solution": "An integer $a$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $n$ if and only if $a$ and $n$ are coprime, i.e., $\\text{gcd}(a,n)=1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- $11$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(11,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $16$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(16,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- $23$ has a multiplicative inverse modulo $27$ since $\\text{gcd}(23,27)=1.\\,\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
